This project contains code used to estimate a discrete choice land-use model and site-specific WTA payments to irrigators for agricultural water conservation as part of the paper 'Incentivizing Water Conservation in Agriculture: A Case Study of the Great Salt Lake Watersheds'.
Citation Man Li and Asif Ahmed Khan 2025 Environ. Res. Lett. 20 014063
DOI 10.1088/1748-9326/ad99e8

First script: Water_WTA.R
Code used to 
 - estimate a discrete choice land-use model
 - apply the model to estimate site-specific WTA payments, water-saving potential, and unit conservation cost
 - develop two payment systems for agricultural conservation under the baseline scenario and a conservative scenario

Second script: Mapping.R
Code used to map Figs 1, 2, 4, and 5.

Data can be accessed at https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.28339361
